  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;be the distance between the foot of perpendiculars of the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;on the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "26",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>so points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lie on same side of the given plane.</p><p>Perpendicular&nbsp;distance of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;from the plane is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Perpendicular distance of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;from&nbsp;the plane is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is parallel to given plane. So, distance between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;distance between their foot of perpendiculars.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>26</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mover><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"
  }
}